  <ctml:notes>Four-player single-elimination knockout at the Saint Louis Chess Club, 22-27 August 2026, played strictly from the chess.com broadcast (no ChessResults record was located). Bracket: semifinals SF-A (Keymer vs Praggnanandhaa) and SF-B (So vs Caruana) on 22-24 Aug; the final (Caruana vs Praggnanandhaa) and third-place match (Keymer vs So) on 25-27 Aug. Each match is two classical games, two rapid, and four blitz, scored classical 6/3, rapid 4/2, blitz 2/1 (win/draw); when both classical games are drawn the players contest a bonus blitz game (tagged segment:blitz-bonus), which scores as an ordinary blitz game. Weighted match results: SF-A Praggnanandhaa 19-9 Keymer; SF-B Caruana 18-12 So; final Praggnanandhaa 15-13 Caruana; third place So 18-12 Keymer. Final standings: 1 Praggnanandhaa, 2 Caruana, 3 So, 4 Keymer. Player federations were resolved from the in-source FIDE ids (not present in the chess.com PGN). The knockout is represented with the CTML 2.1 bracket model (stages -&gt; ties -&gt; legs, one leg per game) and participant placement; each game also carries a segment tag (classical/rapid/blitz/blitz-bonus). Each leg's scores are the weighted points that game contributed, so a tie's legs sum to its match points. Every played game, move, and per-move clock is stored losslessly. No engine evaluations were present in the source, so no eval elements were invented.</ctml:notes>
